                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "In this video I take a look at Robosoul: From the Depths of Pax Animi an FPS action adventure game.\nFirst I saw the really cheap price and though \"Hmm, probably not going to be too good.\" Then I played it and was left with my mouth a gape. This game is fantastic! \nThe story itself is quite amazing and well crafted but the game play also well exceeded expectations. \nWe have a boy who's soul has been digitized after his mothers death and he can now switch between worlds, reality and the digital world. In the digital world he can help either his mother who is now forced to process information for the bad guys as a computer program and in the real world his dad who is still alive but battling robots that have been possessed by the bad guys and began attacking. In the real world he possesses a robot as well for a physical form.\nIt's surreal, entertaining, fun, and very well crafted. At this price you'd have rock's in your head to pass on it.\n\nWatch the video to see what the game is like.....\nhttps://youtu.be/Rb6srNxgI1w\nCheck'n Games, providing you with as many Let's Play's as we can.\nThanks for watching. Please like comment and subscribe.",
